        "original_id": "7eeb500a-4c8d-5dd1-8084-cee66fb8ed46",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Valparaiso University, Old Dominion University, College of William & Mary, Concordia Seminary, Philippine Christian University, New York Yankees\n- People: Oswald Hoffmann, Bud Metheny\n- Places: Norfolk, Virginia, Hampton Roads, Valparaiso, Indiana, Manila, Philippines\n- Concepts: honorary degrees, university enrollment, campus size\n\nFacts:\n- Old Dominion University was established in 1930 as the Norfolk Division of the College of William & Mary.\n- Bud Metheny played professional baseball for the New York Yankees from 1943 to 1946.\n- Bud Metheny served Old Dominion University for 32 years as head baseball coach, head basketball coach, and athletic director.\n- Old Dominion University is a public, co-educational research university in Norfolk, Virginia, with two satellite campuses in the Hampton Roads area.\n- Old Dominion University had an enrollment of 24,670 students in the 2014–2015 academic year and is one of the largest universities in Virginia.\n- Valparaiso University, commonly known as Valpo, is a coeducational four-year Lutheran institution with about 4,500 students from more than 50 countries on a 350-acre campus.\n- Oswald Hoffmann held honorary degrees from Concordia Seminary, Valparaiso University in Valparaiso, Indiana, and Philippine Christian University in Manila, Philippines.",
